From 050e8b1cce5f7c0a52e7f4a03e0691c47d542025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:09:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 679/681] feat(v1): act on a loop by where it is, and follow the
 reasoning parser's markers

Base: candidate-37's patch head 5b7cfa37f (vLLM tree af0fb152), on 0656
and 0674 (#787, #845).

Rationale. 0674 made loop detection the default everywhere, with the
thresholds tuned for reasoning (a 24-token span). Inside reasoning the
action is mild: the reasoning ends and the model answers. In the visible
answer the action stops the request, and legitimate answers repeat too: a
zero-filled array, a table rule, a file written through a tool call. An
operator found 199-token runs of one token in legitimate messages whose
distinct-token ratio was 0.82-0.84 (#787, comment 6564709937). The
handling now depends on where the loop is:

- inside reasoning: break at the first loop, as before; a forced end that
  has not landed within FORCED_REASONING_END_GRACE (64) output tokens stops
  the request instead of leaving the loop unchecked until max_tokens;
- in the answer after a reasoning loop: stop at the first loop (the context
  is already degenerate);
- in the answer of a request whose reasoning did not loop: stop token soup
  (one token over 60% of the answer's last 512 tokens, in a run or more
  every 32 tokens) once it has persisted OUTPUT_SOUP_PERSIST (256) tokens
  past its first detection; stop any other loop only after
  OUTPUT_LOOP_PERSIST (2048) tokens, and only if it leaves fewer than one
  distinct token in ten among the answer's last 512 tokens. Detections up
  to OUTPUT_LOOP_GAP (64) tokens apart count as one loop. Legitimate
  periodic output is long at real token counts (a 256-zero C array is 780
  tokens, a 16x16 matrix 792), and a soak on hardware stopped a 128-zero
  array at its 292nd of 396 tokens under a single 256-token horizon.

A token-soup rule joins the detector: one token at 60% or more of the last
32-64 tokens, with at most one distinct token per eight. It catches the
production collapse ("11x Vila, Estud compar, 9x Vila, ..."), whose runs
are shorter than the contiguous rules need and whose period is irregular.

Request.update_reasoning_markers follows DeepSeekV4Parser's transitions:
inside reasoning only the end marker leaves, so a repeated start marker no
longer restarts the loop window or cancels a forced end; in the answer a
start marker opens reasoning again and a stray end marker is answer text,
so it no longer moves the answer's start (which let a loop with end markers
in it evade detection). A client's repetition_detection now adds to the
built-in detection in the answer instead of replacing it.

The scheduler logs one line when an answer loop is first suspected, with
the request's answer start, thinking_disabled and loop breaks, so a missed
loop can be explained from the log.

Quality implications. Sampling is unchanged: check_stop only reads
committed tokens, so a request that never loops gets the same tokens and
the same finish. Requests that loop in the answer run longer before they
stop (a single-token run inside varied output stops once it dominates the
answer's last 512 tokens, within 512 tokens of its start); requests whose
legitimate answer repeats are no longer cut. Replayed over 3,618 chunks
(5.84M tokens) of real code and documentation as visible answers,
candidate-37 stops 31 and this stops none; as reasoning both break 31, and
the token-soup rule adds none. Replayed with the real tokenizer, legitimate
repetition up to about 2,000 tokens is kept ('hello' 200 times, 128-, 256-
and 512-zero arrays, a 16x16 matrix, separators, a 200-row table; candidate-37
stops each within 37 tokens); the production soup stops 415 tokens after it
starts and an exactly periodic runaway after about 2,070. The detector costs 8.1 us a token against
7.7 us (single core, recorded outputs).

Tests. tests/v1/core/test_repetition_detection.py: token soup (the
incident shape, interjections of new tokens, alternations and prose that
must not match), the parser-following markers, the forced-end grace, the
answer's two horizons and diversity, and known trigger shapes (the
production soup, separator rules of 199 and 300 tokens in varied output,
requested repetition at real token counts: 200 words, a 512-zero array, a
16x16 matrix, a 200-row table; the "Let me do it." stall). The scheduler and output suites fail exactly as they do on
candidate-37 (the offline hub lacks facebook/opt-125m).

Upstream status: local, on the local patches 0656 and 0674; not submitted.
